meta {
  name: List Bulk Emails
  type: http
  seq: 7
}

get {
  url: {{notificationsBaseUrl}}/api/v1/notifications/bulk-email?page=1&size=20
  body: none
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  page: 1
  size: 20
  ~status: Completed
  ~search: registration
  ~from: 2026-09-01T00:00:00Z
  ~to: 2026-09-30T23:59:59Z
}

docs {
  The bulk-email list — one row per SEND, newest first, not one row per recipient.
  A 3,000-recipient circular is a single entry here with sent/failed/suppressed counts.
  Open Get Bulk Email Recipients for the per-person breakdown.

  Only bulk jobs appear. OTPs, password-setup and application-decision mails share the
  underlying OutboundEmails table but have no BulkEmailJobs row, and every query here
  joins through BulkEmailJobs — so transactional mail can never surface on this endpoint.

  Query params (all optional, ANDed):
    page   - default 1; a value < 1 is treated as 1
    size   - default 20; clamped to 1..100 in the handler (out-of-range is coerced, not rejected)
    status - Draft | Resolving | Processing | Completed | PartiallyFailed | Failed
             (the JOB status enum). Bound by name. An unknown value is a bare 400 from
             model binding, NOT the standard envelope.
    search - case-insensitive LIKE against the job subject
    from   - ISO 8601; filters createdDate >= from
    to     - ISO 8601; filters createdDate <= to

  Success (200): data is a PagedResult of BulkEmailJobListItemDto:
    jobGuid, subject, status, totalRecipients, sentCount, failedCount,
    suppressedCount, hasAttachment, createdDate, completedDate.

  totalRecipients is the count of GUIDs that RESOLVED to an address, which is lower than
  the "selectedRecipients" the create call returned. The three counters are recomputed on
  an interval (OutboundEmail:RollUpEveryTicks, default every 10 ticks) so they can lag a
  live send by ~10s; terminal values are always correct.

  An empty result is a 200 with items: [], totalCount: 0 — never a 404.
  401 unauthorized - no valid erp_access cookie.
}
